  "[0-9]{1,12}\.[0-9]{2}|[0-9]{1,12}" — either exactly two decimals or no
  decimal point at all. "100.5" matches neither alternative, so the document is
  rejected. Every amount the builder emits must carry exactly two decimals.

  Element under test: detalleCompras/baseImponible, ats.xsd:741.
  This is the §5.4 decimal-pattern trap; it is a pure grammar rule, so unlike
  the cases below the SRI norm and the XSD agree.
-->
